<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodorus of Cyrene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodorus of Cyrene was a Greek mathematician of the 5th century BCE, a teacher of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plato">Plato</a> and of Theaetetus. In Plato's dialogue Theaetetus he is credited with showing that the square roots of the non-square numbers from 3 to 17 are irrational. He is among the earliest known contributors to the theory of incommensurable magnitudes.</p></div>
